= Web Ontology Language — Simple =

'''OWL''' is a language for writing formal ontologies for the Web.

It lets you describe:

* classes of things;
* individual things;
* relationships;
* rules about those relationships.

For example, you could say:

<pre>
Dog is a kind of Mammal
Fido is a Dog
</pre>

A reasoner can then infer:

<pre>
Fido is a Mammal
</pre>

OWL can also describe stronger rules such as:
* two classes cannot overlap;
* one relation is transitive;
* two names refer to the same individual.

OWL is related to [[Resource Description Framework/Simple|RDF]], but RDF and OWL are not the same thing.

